Package: surtgeoharmonizer
Type: Project
Title: Auditable Administrative-Scale Earth-Data Harmonization and Provenance Labelling
Version: 1.3.0
Authors@R: person("Audre Prince", "Tuyishime", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "priplee@gmail.com",
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0002-0799-3140"))
Description: Open R and Python command-line workflow for converting
    heterogeneous environmental rasters into consistent administrative-unit
    GeoJSON layers with explicit provenance, fail-closed evidence
    classification, provider-specific reference builders, controlled
    transformation fixtures, generic-region examples, failure-injection tests,
    independent release-contract validation, and scoped public-data numerical
    reproduction. Rwanda is the reference implementation rather than a
    hard-coded software boundary.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Imports:
    exactextractr (>= 0.10.1),
    jsonlite (>= 2.0.0),
    sf (>= 1.1.1),
    terra (>= 1.9.27)
